WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.281 --> 00:00:02.864
(techno music)

00:00:03.721 --> 00:00:06.571
- [Leon] Jai alai is a dance.

00:00:06.571 --> 00:00:08.681
- [Benny] This is a game of finesse.

00:00:08.681 --> 00:00:13.681
It's fast, the balls go between
150 and 170 miles per hour.

00:00:13.725 --> 00:00:15.498
- [Narrator] For the better
part of the 20th century,

00:00:15.498 --> 00:00:17.676
jai alai was the sport in Miami.

00:00:17.676 --> 00:00:19.448
You went to see it and to be seen.

00:00:19.448 --> 00:00:22.411
Yet today, the sport is barely hanging on.

00:00:22.411 --> 00:00:23.828
So, what happened?

00:00:29.549 --> 00:00:31.966
(soft music)

00:00:33.576 --> 00:00:35.476
- Jai alai's a sport that was very famous

00:00:35.476 --> 00:00:36.891
back in the ’40s, ’50s,

00:00:36.891 --> 00:00:40.102
and it comes from Europe, Spain, France.

00:00:40.102 --> 00:00:42.519
In 1924, it arrived in Miami.

00:00:45.513 --> 00:00:47.686
- [News Anchor] Jai alai, one
of the oldest of all games,

00:00:47.686 --> 00:00:51.334
is taking winter residents
of Miami by storm.

00:00:51.334 --> 00:00:53.519
- [Narrator] It's been dubbed
the world’s fastest game.

00:00:53.519 --> 00:00:55.210
You may have vague memories of seeing it

00:00:55.210 --> 00:00:56.602
in a Dos Equis commercial,

00:00:56.602 --> 00:00:58.721
or in the opening scene of “Miami Vice.”

00:00:58.721 --> 00:01:00.264
- [Benny] It was an exciting sport,

00:01:00.264 --> 00:01:02.392
and we used to get a lot of celebrities

00:01:02.392 --> 00:01:04.196
that would come out and
wanna be a part of it,

00:01:04.196 --> 00:01:06.229
and wanna be seen at jai alai.

00:01:06.229 --> 00:01:07.505
- [Narrator] That's Benny Bueno.

00:01:07.505 --> 00:01:08.851
He's one of the most decorated American

00:01:08.851 --> 00:01:11.181
jai alai players of all time.

00:01:11.181 --> 00:01:13.986
He's currently the player
manager at Dania Casino.

00:01:13.986 --> 00:01:16.631
- It was a combination of the nightlife,

00:01:16.631 --> 00:01:20.130
and getting dressed up
and having a place to go.

00:01:20.130 --> 00:01:22.523
The largest crowd that
ever visited Miami Jai Alai

00:01:22.523 --> 00:01:24.097
was 15,000 people.

00:01:24.097 --> 00:01:27.180
The arena held probably about 12,000.

00:01:28.413 --> 00:01:30.355
It's just something that's
visually stimulating

00:01:30.355 --> 00:01:32.768
for someone that's never seen it.

00:01:32.768 --> 00:01:34.935
It's addicting in a sense.

00:01:36.218 --> 00:01:40.177
- I've been playing jai alai for 28 years.

00:01:40.177 --> 00:01:44.516
I got to experience a good
five years of 7,000-8,000 people

00:01:44.516 --> 00:01:46.122
in the fronton.

00:01:46.122 --> 00:01:48.599
It was so loud, you couldn't
really hear your partners.

00:01:48.599 --> 00:01:53.349
And it was just awesome to
play in front of a huge crowd.

00:01:55.932 --> 00:01:58.467
- [Narrator] Now, the inevitable question:

00:01:58.467 --> 00:02:01.030
How did we go from crowds of 10,000 plus

00:02:01.030 --> 00:02:03.142
to a scattered 100 on a good day?

00:02:03.142 --> 00:02:05.614
- I believe it was in the mid-thirties,

00:02:05.614 --> 00:02:08.904
that gambling was legalized on jai alai.

00:02:08.904 --> 00:02:11.768
The wagering on jai alai
has always been a blessing

00:02:11.768 --> 00:02:14.688
and a curse—in the
sense where the wagering

00:02:14.688 --> 00:02:17.702
is what has kept it alive for so long,

00:02:17.702 --> 00:02:21.737
but it has kind of taken away
a little bit of the sport,

00:02:21.737 --> 00:02:24.487
the athleticism, the game itself.

00:02:25.432 --> 00:02:27.821
Over the years, the focus has changed.

00:02:27.821 --> 00:02:30.229
It's no longer a jai alai arena,

00:02:30.229 --> 00:02:34.348
it is a casino, with a jai alai
arena, with a poker room.

00:02:34.348 --> 00:02:37.351
And the focus is mainly on the property

00:02:37.351 --> 00:02:39.540
rather just the sport of jai alai.

00:02:39.540 --> 00:02:41.705
- [Narrator] But that wasn't
the sports only problem.

00:02:41.705 --> 00:02:44.836
In 1981, then owner of World
Jai Alai, Roger Wheeler,

00:02:44.836 --> 00:02:46.381
was assassinated.

00:02:46.381 --> 00:02:48.201
His murder is associated
with Whitey Bulger

00:02:48.201 --> 00:02:50.050
and the Winter Hill Gang.

00:02:50.050 --> 00:02:52.781
And the sport became inexorably
tied to organized crime

00:02:52.781 --> 00:02:54.369
in the public’s mind.

00:02:54.369 --> 00:02:56.511
Then, in 1988, there was a player strike

00:02:56.511 --> 00:02:58.511
that lasted three years.

00:02:59.950 --> 00:03:02.851
- It all was the perfect
storm, where it started

00:03:02.851 --> 00:03:05.914
to take some of our clientele away.

00:03:05.914 --> 00:03:08.317
I don't want it to be on my watch

00:03:08.317 --> 00:03:11.474
that jai alai goes away or fails.

00:03:11.474 --> 00:03:14.144
It's a lot of fun, and
it's something that I did

00:03:14.144 --> 00:03:17.537
for 25 years, so I can't just walk away.

00:03:17.537 --> 00:03:20.169
- Looking out at the crowd
and seeing less people

00:03:20.169 --> 00:03:22.450
doesn't deter my work ethic.

00:03:22.450 --> 00:03:24.259
- Go right, go right.

00:03:24.259 --> 00:03:27.932
- I'm gonna play the same
level and prepare myself,

00:03:27.932 --> 00:03:31.176
whether its 1,000 people or ...

00:03:31.176 --> 00:03:32.550
200 people.

00:03:32.550 --> 00:03:34.689
Once the balls in the air, you gotta move.

00:03:34.689 --> 00:03:39.053
Playing a sport at that
speed every day, you know, is awesome.

00:03:39.053 --> 00:03:42.970
I still have the love and
the passion for the game.

